################################################################################
#  orchestration.auth
#  Face Liveness + PAD orchestration for the MOSIP Android Registration Client
#
#  Covers : Resident face capture · Operator auth · Supervisor auth
#  Stack  : Flutter (Dart UI) · Pigeon bridge · Native Java layer · CameraX /
#           SBI device adapters · TFLite/MediaPipe engine · Android Keystore
#  Status : Design spec. Items tagged [VERIFY] must be confirmed against the
#           mosip/android-registration-client repo and the device vendor's SBI.
################################################################################


================================================================================
1. PURPOSE
================================================================================
One orchestrator drives liveness for all three workflows so behaviour is
identical online/offline and across roles.

  Liveness is a GATE placed in front of the existing capture / authentication
  step. It never replaces device capture or biometric matching.

  gate result  = PASS | FAIL | ABORTED | BLOCKED
  PASS yields  = LivenessResult { sessionId, evidence, bestFrameRef }
  Downstream   = existing capture (SBI) or existing match (Biometric SDK / auth)
                 runs ONLY after PASS and ONLY inside the same session window.

Design rules:
  R1  Fail closed. Exception, timeout, missing/invalid model => FAIL, never skip.
  R2  Frames never cross the Pigeon channel. Preview uses a Flutter Texture.
  R3  The user never selects a challenge. Orchestrator selects (SecureRandom).
  R4  No decision depends on network. Config/model are cached locally.
  R5  UI receives generic messages; PAD detail goes to audit/diagnostics only.


================================================================================
2. COMPONENTS AND RESPONSIBILITIES
================================================================================

  Layer     Component                    Responsibility
  --------  ---------------------------  ---------------------------------------
  Dart      LivenessScreen / ViewModel   Render state, prompts, retry UI; send
                                         start/cancel commands only
  Bridge    LivenessHostApi (Pigeon)     Dart -> Java commands
  Bridge    LivenessFlutterApi (Pigeon)  Java -> Dart events/state
  Native    LivenessOrchestrator         State machine, attempt/retry counting,
                                         timers, session binding, audit
  Native    LivenessPolicyProvider       Resolve effective policy per role
  Native    FaceFrameSource (interface)  Deliver frames (CameraX, SBI, Mock)
  Native    FaceAnalyzer (interface)     Face count, quality, pose, eyes, smile
  Native    LivenessEngine (interface)   Passive score + PAD + action verify
  Native    ChallengeSelector            Random, non-repeating challenge sequence
  Native    PreviewTextureBridge         Push frames to Flutter TextureRegistry
  Native    LivenessEvidenceSigner       Sign evidence with Android Keystore key
  Native    ModelStore                   Signed models, version, rollback
  Native    AuditBridge                  Write events to existing audit manager
  Existing  SBI intent client            Final signed face capture      [VERIFY]
  Existing  Biometric SDK                1:1 match (offline operator)   [VERIFY]


================================================================================
3. POLICY (CONFIGURATION SCHEMA)
================================================================================
Source: existing global-param / config-sync framework, cached in local DB.
        Keys prefixed:  mosip.registration.liveness.*          [VERIFY mechanism]
Resolution: workflow-specific key > common key > built-in safe default.

--- effective policy object (after resolution) ---
policy:
  version: "2026-10-01.3"            # recorded in every evidence record
  enabled: true
  passive:
    threshold: 0.80                  # 0..1
    windowFrames: 10                 # median over last N quality-passing frames
    minValidFrames: 6                # frames needed before a decision
    decisionTimeoutSec: 6            # no decision by then => attempt fails
  active:
    enabled: true
    minChallenges: 1                 # supervisor default: 2
    challengeTypes: [BLINK, SMILE, TURN_LEFT, TURN_RIGHT]
    challengeTimeoutSec: 8
  maxRetries: 3
  onRepeatedFailure: BLOCK           # BLOCK | FALLBACK_OTHER_MODALITY |
                                     # LOCKOUT_TEMPORARY | SUPERVISOR_EXCEPTION
  lockoutSeconds: 120                # used by LOCKOUT_TEMPORARY
  quality:
    maxFaces: 1
    minFaceAreaRatio: 0.15
    maxYawDeg: 15                    # for passive/neutral phase
    maxPitchDeg: 15

--- built-in security floor (code constants, cannot be lowered by config) ---
  passive.threshold          >= 0.60
  maxRetries                 <= 5
  challengeTimeoutSec        in [3, 20]
  supervisor.enabled=false   => ignored unless build flag ALLOW_DISABLE_LIVENESS
  invalid/missing value      => use safe default + audit "CONFIG_INVALID"

--- suggested defaults per role ---
  RESIDENT  : as above
  OPERATOR  : as above
  SUPERVISOR: active.minChallenges = 2, onRepeatedFailure = BLOCK


================================================================================
4. STATE MACHINE
================================================================================

States
  IDLE
  INITIALIZING          open frame source, load model, create session+nonce
  POSITIONING           wait for exactly one acceptable face (quality gate)
  PASSIVE_EVALUATING    collect window, compute score + PAD
  CHALLENGE_PROMPT      show selected action
  CHALLENGE_VERIFYING   analyse frames for action + re-run PAD/score
  CHALLENGE_PASSED      one challenge done; more required? -> next prompt
  ATTEMPT_FAILED        record failure reason, decide retry/terminal
  RETRY_WAIT            short pause, new session nonce + new challenge sequence
  PASSED                gate satisfied; hand off to capture/match
  TERMINAL_FAILURE      retries exhausted -> onRepeatedFailure mode
  DEVICE_ERROR          device/camera/frame failure (not an attempt)
  ABORTED               user cancel / lifecycle (app background)

Transitions (guard -> action)
  IDLE                -> INITIALIZING         start(role, workflow)
  INITIALIZING        -> POSITIONING          source+model ready
  INITIALIZING        -> DEVICE_ERROR         source/model failure (fail closed)
  POSITIONING         -> PASSIVE_EVALUATING   >= minValidFrames good frames
  POSITIONING         -> POSITIONING          no/multiple/poor face (emit hint,
                                              NOT counted as attempt)
  PASSIVE_EVALUATING  -> ATTEMPT_FAILED       padAttackDetected
  PASSIVE_EVALUATING  -> PASSED               score >= threshold && !pad
  PASSIVE_EVALUATING  -> CHALLENGE_PROMPT     score < threshold && active.enabled
  PASSIVE_EVALUATING  -> ATTEMPT_FAILED       score < threshold && !active.enabled
  PASSIVE_EVALUATING  -> ATTEMPT_FAILED       decisionTimeout
  CHALLENGE_PROMPT    -> CHALLENGE_VERIFYING  prompt shown, baseline captured
  CHALLENGE_VERIFYING -> CHALLENGE_PASSED     action verified && !pad && score ok
  CHALLENGE_VERIFYING -> ATTEMPT_FAILED       padAttackDetected | timeout |
                                              wrong action | face lost > 2 s
  CHALLENGE_PASSED    -> CHALLENGE_PROMPT     completed < minChallenges
  CHALLENGE_PASSED    -> PASSED               completed >= minChallenges
  ATTEMPT_FAILED      -> RETRY_WAIT           attempts < maxRetries
  ATTEMPT_FAILED      -> TERMINAL_FAILURE     attempts >= maxRetries
  RETRY_WAIT          -> INITIALIZING         (fresh session)
  any                 -> DEVICE_ERROR         3 consecutive invalid frames |
                                              disconnect | camera revoked
  DEVICE_ERROR        -> INITIALIZING         user taps retry (attempt unchanged)
  any                 -> ABORTED              cancel() | onPause beyond grace

Invariants
  - attemptCount increments ONLY on ATTEMPT_FAILED.
  - Every new attempt gets a new sessionId, nonce and challenge sequence.
  - PASSED is valid for validitySec (default 30). After expiry, capture/match
    must be refused and the gate re-run.
  - Orchestrator state is single-threaded (one serial executor); engine and
    source callbacks post into it.


================================================================================
5. SEQUENCE DIAGRAMS (Mermaid)
================================================================================

--- 5.1 Resident face capture (passive pass) ---
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant UI as Flutter UI
  participant B as Pigeon
  participant O as LivenessOrchestrator
  participant S as FaceFrameSource
  participant E as LivenessEngine
  participant D as SBI Capture (existing)
  UI->>B: startSession(role=RESIDENT)
  B->>O: start()
  O->>O: resolve policy, new session+nonce
  O->>S: open()
  S-->>O: frames (continuous)
  O->>E: analyze(frame)
  E-->>O: quality, passiveScore, padFlags
  O-->>UI: state=PASSIVE_EVALUATING ("Checking face liveness…")
  O->>O: score>=threshold && !pad
  O-->>UI: state=PASSED
  UI->>D: capture face (existing flow)
  D-->>UI: signed face
  O->>O: binding check (session window, consistency)
  UI->>UI: accept face
```

--- 5.2 Passive fails -> active challenge -> retry ---
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant UI as Flutter UI
  participant O as Orchestrator
  participant E as Engine
  participant C as ChallengeSelector
  O->>E: analyze(frames)
  E-->>O: score 0.55 (< 0.80), pad=none
  O->>C: select(types, min=1, exclude=last)
  C-->>O: [TURN_LEFT]
  O-->>UI: state=CHALLENGE_PROMPT ("Please turn your head to the left")
  loop until timeout
    O->>E: verifyAction(TURN_LEFT, frame)
    E-->>O: progress / detected / pad re-check
    O-->>UI: feedback ("Please continue" / "Action detected" / "Hold still")
  end
  alt verified
    O-->>UI: PASSED
  else failed/timeout/pad
    O-->>UI: ATTEMPT_FAILED (retriesLeft=n)
    O->>O: RETRY_WAIT -> new session & new challenge
  end
```

--- 5.3 Operator / Supervisor authentication (online or offline) ---
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant UI as Flutter UI
  participant O as Orchestrator
  participant D as SBI Capture (existing)
  participant M as Biometric SDK / Auth service
  participant A as Audit
  UI->>O: startSession(role=OPERATOR|SUPERVISOR, userId)
  O->>O: policy(role) ; liveness gate (passive -> active if needed)
  O-->>UI: PASSED
  UI->>D: capture face
  D-->>UI: signed face
  O->>O: verify session valid && consistency(bestFrame, signedFace)
  UI->>M: match (local templates if offline, auth service if online)
  M-->>UI: match result
  UI->>UI: authenticated = livenessPassed AND matchPassed
  O->>A: LIVENESS_* + AUTH_* events (signed evidence)
```
Supervisor extra rule: supervisorUserId != currently logged-in operatorUserId.


================================================================================
6. NATIVE INTERFACES (Java)
================================================================================

public interface FaceFrameSource {
    SourceCapabilities capabilities();            // fps, resolutions, formats,
                                                  // signed?, hasIrDepth?
    void open(SourceConfig cfg, FrameListener l) throws DeviceException;
    void close();
    interface FrameListener {
        void onFrame(FaceFrame frame);            // never blocks; engine drops old
        void onSourceError(DeviceError error);    // DISCONNECTED, PERMISSION, INVALID_FRAME...
    }
}

public final class FaceFrame {
    long timestampNanos; int width, height, rotationDeg;
    FrameFormat format;                           // YUV_420_888 | NV21 | JPEG | RGBA
    byte[] data /* or buffer ref */; boolean mirrored; String sourceId;
}

public interface FaceAnalyzer {
    FaceObservation analyze(FaceFrame f);         // faceCount, bbox, yaw/pitch/roll,
                                                  // eyeOpenL/R, smileProb, landmarks,
                                                  // quality{blur, luminance, areaRatio}
}

public interface LivenessEngine {
    EngineInfo info();                            // name, version, modelVersion,
                                                  // supportedChallenges, certified?
    void init(ModelRef model) throws EngineException;
    PassiveResult passive(FaceFrame f, FaceObservation o);   // score + PadFlags
    ActionProgress verifyAction(Challenge c, ActionContext ctx,
                                FaceFrame f, FaceObservation o);
    void release();
}

public interface LivenessPolicyProvider {
    LivenessPolicy resolve(Role role, Workflow workflow);
}

public interface ChallengeSelector {
    List<Challenge> select(Set<ChallengeType> pool, int min, ChallengeType lastUsed);
}

public interface LivenessOrchestrator {
    SessionHandle start(Role role, Workflow workflow, String userIdOrNull);
    void cancel(String sessionId);
    LivenessResult currentResult(String sessionId);   // null unless PASSED+valid
    void setListener(LivenessListener l);             // events -> Pigeon FlutterApi
}

Enums
  Role           : RESIDENT | OPERATOR | SUPERVISOR
  ChallengeType  : BLINK | SMILE | TURN_LEFT | TURN_RIGHT | LOOK_UP | LOOK_DOWN
  FailReason     : PAD_DETECTED | LOW_LIVENESS | CHALLENGE_FAILED |
                   CHALLENGE_TIMEOUT | DECISION_TIMEOUT
  DeviceError    : DEVICE_UNAVAILABLE | DISCONNECTED | CAMERA_UNAVAILABLE |
                   PERMISSION_DENIED | INVALID_FRAME | ENGINE_ERROR
  Hint           : NO_FACE | MULTIPLE_FACES | TOO_FAR | TOO_DARK | BLURRY |
                   LOOK_STRAIGHT | HOLD_STILL


================================================================================
7. PIGEON API (Dart <-> Java)   [VERIFY existing pigeon file conventions]
================================================================================

class LivenessStateEvent {
  String sessionId;
  String state;              // enum name from section 4
  String? challenge;         // current challenge type
  String? hint;              // Hint enum name
  String? uiMessageKey;      // localisation key, NOT raw text
  int attemptsUsed;
  int attemptsMax;
  int? challengeIndex;       // 1-based
  int? challengeTotal;
  double? progress;          // 0..1 for UI ring (no raw score exposed)
  String? failCategory;      // GENERIC | DEVICE | MAX_RETRIES
}

class LivenessStartResult {
  String sessionId;
  int? previewTextureId;     // Flutter Texture id for live preview
  String? errorCode;
}

class LivenessFinalResult {
  String sessionId;
  String outcome;            // PASSED | TERMINAL_FAILURE | ABORTED
  String? nextAction;        // PROCEED | BLOCK | FALLBACK | LOCKOUT | EXCEPTION
  int? lockoutSeconds;
  int validForSeconds;       // gate validity window when PASSED
}

@HostApi()
abstract class LivenessHostApi {
  @async LivenessStartResult startSession(String role, String workflow, String? userId);
  void cancelSession(String sessionId);
  @async LivenessFinalResult awaitResult(String sessionId);   // optional; events suffice
  Map<String, String> diagnosticsSnapshot();                  // diagnostic mode only
}

@FlutterApi()
abstract class LivenessFlutterApi {
  void onState(LivenessStateEvent event);
  void onFinal(LivenessFinalResult result);
}

Notes
  - uiMessageKey maps to localised strings (supports i18n and per-deployment text).
  - Raw passive scores / PAD flags are NOT sent to Dart unless diagnostic mode
    is enabled (R5).
  - Preview: native pushes frames to a TextureRegistry.SurfaceTextureEntry; Dart
    shows Texture(textureId). Face-box/oval overlays drawn in Dart from normalised
    coordinates sent at <= 10 Hz (optional field).


================================================================================
8. ORCHESTRATOR PSEUDO-CODE
================================================================================

start(role, workflow, userId):
    policy = policyProvider.resolve(role, workflow)
    if !policy.enabled and !BUILD.ALLOW_DISABLE_LIVENESS:  policy.enabled = true
    if !policy.enabled: return PASSED_BYPASSED (audited, evidence.bypassed=true)
    attempts = 0
    runAttempt()

runAttempt():
    s = newSession(nonce = secureRandom(16), start = now())
    audit(LIVENESS_STARTED, s, policy.version)
    try:
        engine.init(modelStore.activeModel())            # verifies hash/signature
        source.open(cfg, onFrame)
    catch -> transition(DEVICE_ERROR); return            # fail closed

onFrame(f):                                              # runs on analysis thread,
    post(serialExecutor):                                # dropped if busy
        obs = analyzer.analyze(f)
        switch state:
          POSITIONING:
            hint = qualityGate(obs, policy.quality)
            if hint != null: emit(hint) ; return
            if ++goodFrames >= policy.passive.minValidFrames:
                transition(PASSIVE_EVALUATING)
          PASSIVE_EVALUATING:
            r = engine.passive(f, obs)
            window.add(r.score) ; padSeen |= r.pad.attackDetected
            if padSeen:                   fail(PAD_DETECTED); return
            if window.size >= policy.passive.windowFrames:
                score = median(window)
                if score >= policy.passive.threshold: pass(); return
                if policy.active.enabled: beginActive()
                else: fail(LOW_LIVENESS)
            if elapsed > decisionTimeoutSec: fail(DECISION_TIMEOUT)
          CHALLENGE_VERIFYING:
            p = engine.verifyAction(current, ctx, f, obs)
            r = engine.passive(f, obs)                    # re-evaluate PAD/liveness
            if r.pad.attackDetected:      fail(PAD_DETECTED); return
            if p.done:                    challengeDone()
            elif p.wrongAction:           fail(CHALLENGE_FAILED)
            elif now() > challengeDeadline: fail(CHALLENGE_TIMEOUT)
            else: emit(progress/feedback)

beginActive():
    seq = challengeSelector.select(policy.active.challengeTypes ∩
                                   engine.info().supportedChallenges,
                                   policy.active.minChallenges, lastUsedThisDevice)
    if seq.isEmpty(): fail(CHALLENGE_FAILED) (config error, audited)
    session.sequence = seq ; idx = 0 ; promptNext()

challengeDone():
    if ++idx >= seq.size(): pass() else promptNext()

pass():
    best = bestFrameOfSession()
    evidence = signer.sign({sessionId, nonce, role, userId?, policy.version,
        engine.info(), modelVersion, passiveScore(median), challenges+results,
        timings, bestFrameSha256, deviceId, ts})
    session.validUntil = now() + validitySec
    transition(PASSED) ; audit(LIVENESS_PASSED, evidence)
    source.close()                         # frames released from memory

fail(reason):
    attempts++ ; audit(LIVENESS_FAILED, reason)          # PAD detail only here
    source.close()
    if attempts >= policy.maxRetries: terminal()
    else: transition(RETRY_WAIT) -> runAttempt()          # new session/challenge

terminal():
    apply policy.onRepeatedFailure:
        BLOCK                    -> nextAction=BLOCK
        FALLBACK_OTHER_MODALITY  -> nextAction=FALLBACK (only OPERATOR/SUPERVISOR,
                                    only if another modality is configured)
        LOCKOUT_TEMPORARY        -> persist lockoutUntil (survives app restart)
        SUPERVISOR_EXCEPTION     -> nextAction=EXCEPTION (RESIDENT only; audited)
    audit(LIVENESS_TERMINAL_FAILURE)

Consume gate downstream:
    isGateValid(sessionId) = result.state==PASSED && now()<validUntil
    bindingOk = isGateValid && consistency(bestFrame, signedCapture) >= T_bind
    # T_bind from policy; if no on-device 1:1 matcher available, bindingOk relies
    # on session validity + signed-device capture timing  [VERIFY, see analyse.md R6]


================================================================================
9. ERROR -> ACTION MAP
================================================================================

  Condition                  State            Counts attempt  UI message key
  -------------------------  ---------------  --------------  ------------------------------
  Device unavailable         DEVICE_ERROR     no              liveness.device.unavailable
  Device disconnected        DEVICE_ERROR     no              liveness.device.disconnected
  Camera unavailable/denied  DEVICE_ERROR     no              liveness.camera.unavailable
  Face not detected          POSITIONING      no              liveness.hint.look_camera
  Multiple faces             POSITIONING      no              liveness.hint.single_person
  Poor quality               POSITIONING      no              liveness.hint.lighting/distance
  Score below threshold      -> active        no              liveness.checking -> prompt
  PAD detected               ATTEMPT_FAILED   YES             liveness.pad.generic
  Challenge failed           ATTEMPT_FAILED   YES             liveness.failed.try_again
  Challenge timeout          ATTEMPT_FAILED   YES             liveness.failed.try_again
  Max retries                TERMINAL_FAILURE -               liveness.max_retries.recovery
  Invalid frames (3 in row)  DEVICE_ERROR     no              liveness.device.error
  Engine/model error         DEVICE_ERROR     no              liveness.unavailable (fail closed)

Default English strings (localisable)
  liveness.checking            "Checking face liveness…"
  prompt.blink                 "Please blink"
  prompt.smile                 "Please smile"
  prompt.turn_left             "Please turn your head to the left"
  prompt.turn_right            "Please turn your head to the right"
  feedback.continue            "Please continue"
  feedback.detected            "Action detected"
  feedback.hold                "Hold still"
  success                      "Good, face captured successfully"
  liveness.failed.try_again    "We could not verify face liveness. Please try again."
  liveness.pad.generic         "Face verification could not be completed. Please try again."


================================================================================
10. AUDIT EVENTS (stored locally, synced later)
================================================================================

  Event id               When                      Payload (no images)
  ---------------------  ------------------------  -----------------------------------
  LIVENESS_STARTED       session start             role, workflow, policyVersion, sessionId
  LIVENESS_PASSIVE_DONE  passive decision          medianScore, frames, ms
  LIVENESS_CHALLENGE     per challenge             type, result, ms
  LIVENESS_PASSED        gate passed               evidenceId, totalMs, engine/model ver
  LIVENESS_FAILED        attempt failed            reason, attempt n/max, (PAD detail)
  LIVENESS_TERMINAL      retries exhausted         mode applied
  LIVENESS_DEVICE_ERR    device/camera/engine err  errorCode, sourceId
  LIVENESS_CONFIG_BAD    invalid config            key, fallbackUsed
  LIVENESS_BYPASSED      disabled by policy        role, reason
  LIVENESS_BINDING_FAIL  consistency/window fail   cause
  MODEL_UPDATED          model swap/rollback       old/new version, hash ok

Diagnostic mode (opt-in, local): adds raw scores, per-frame timings, FPS, delegate
used. Still no pixels. Anonymised metrics (avg liveness time, challenge time,
retry rate, failure rate) aggregated without user ids.


================================================================================
11. ADAPTER ORCHESTRATION (VENDOR INDEPENDENCE)
================================================================================

Source selection at start():
    caps = discover()                                  # device capability discovery
    if workflow device has SBI stream      -> SbiStreamFaceSource     [VERIFY]
    else if L0 / built-in camera allowed   -> CameraXFaceSource
    else if dev/test build                 -> MockFaceFrameSource(video)
    else                                   -> DEVICE_ERROR (cannot satisfy liveness)

Dual-source mode (only if device cannot stream):
    liveness frames  <- CameraXFaceSource
    final biometric  <- SBI one-shot signed capture
    link             <- consistency(bestFrame, signedCapture) + same-session window
    (document the weaker trust level; policy flag liveness.requireSignedStream
     can forbid this mode in high-assurance deployments)

Adding a vendor = implement FaceFrameSource (+ optional capability flags). No change
to orchestrator, engine, UI, or policy.

Engine selection:
    engine = EngineRegistry.get(config.engineId)       # "reference-tflite" default
    engine.info().certified is shown in diagnostics and recorded in evidence.


================================================================================
12. THREADING, LIFECYCLE AND RESOURCES
================================================================================

  Threads
    camera/source thread  -> pushes frames (non-blocking)
    analysis thread       -> single HandlerThread; keep-only-latest frame
    orchestrator executor -> single serial executor; owns all state
    main thread           -> Pigeon event delivery only

  Lifecycle
    onPause  > 3 s  -> ABORTED, release camera/engine, audit
    rotation        -> keep session; recompute rotation/mirroring from frame meta
    process death   -> session is not resumable; lockoutUntil persisted in DB

  Resource limits (targets)
    analysis resolution <= 640x480; 10–15 fps; process every 2nd frame if over budget
    inference delegate order: NNAPI/GPU -> XNNPACK CPU
    memory: frames are pooled and zeroed on close; no frame persisted
    window FLAG_SECURE set on liveness screens


================================================================================
13. MODEL AND POLICY UPDATE ORCHESTRATION
================================================================================

  Online:
    sync -> manifest {modelId, version, sha256, signature, minAppVersion}
         -> download to temp -> verify signature + hash -> atomic swap
         -> keep previous version -> health-check inference
         -> on failure auto-rollback + audit MODEL_UPDATED(rollback)
  Offline:
    signed bundle sideload (same verification path)           [bonus]
  Active sessions never switch model mid-session.
  Policy updates apply at the next start() (policy.version recorded per session).


